  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Earthquake Emergency Response Project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project consists of activities relating to disaster relief and the provision of life-preserving services for communities affected by the earthquake that occurred in the highlands region of the Independent State of Papua New Guinea on 26 February 2018, and subsequent aftershocks in the country, including an earthquake on 8 March 2018. These project activities will include, but are not limited to, (i) provision of emergency rescue equipment; ii) provision of relief supplies of water, medical kits, food and shelter; iii) purchase of water purification and sanitation systems; (iv) provision of personal hygiene kits; (v) purchase of emergency communication equipment; (vi) landslide and rubble debris sifting and site clearance to facilitate access; (vii) restoration of critical electricity, water, communication and transport links, and (vili) provision of emergency shelter.</narrative>
  </description>
